id: 1174
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1174, "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "data": {"id": "df4f90a3-ddd4-4118-9d9c-5e8867405716", "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "kind": "text", "position": 1173, "revision": 1174, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"text": "Good, I've read both sub-agent scripts. Now I can see the FFT unit error clearly:\n\n**Line 147**: `fft_freqs = np.fft.rfftfreq(n, d=dt)` where `dt` is in **minutes** → frequencies are in cycles/minute\n**Line 161**: `top_freqs_muhz = top"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:26:30.898977+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:26:31.421979+00:00"}}

id: 1175
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1175, "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "data": {"id": "df4f90a3-ddd4-4118-9d9c-5e8867405716", "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "kind": "text", "position": 1173, "revision": 1175, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"text": "Good, I've read both sub-agent scripts. Now I can see the FFT unit error clearly:\n\n**Line 147**: `fft_freqs = np.fft.rfftfreq(n, d=dt)` where `dt` is in **minutes** → frequencies are in cycles/minute\n**Line 161**: `top_freqs_muhz = top_freqs_hz * 1e6` — treats cycles/minute as Hz and multiplies by 1e6\n\nThe correct conversion from cycles/minute to μHz:\n- 1 cycle/minute = "}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:26:30.898977+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:26:31.937905+00:00"}}

id: 1176
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1176, "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "data": {"id": "df4f90a3-ddd4-4118-9d9c-5e8867405716", "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "kind": "text", "position": 1173, "revision": 1176, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"text": "Good, I've read both sub-agent scripts. Now I can see the FFT unit error clearly:\n\n**Line 147**: `fft_freqs = np.fft.rfftfreq(n, d=dt)` where `dt` is in **minutes** → frequencies are in cycles/minute\n**Line 161**: `top_freqs_muhz = top_freqs_hz * 1e6` — treats cycles/minute as Hz and multiplies by 1e6\n\nThe correct conversion from cycles/minute to μHz:\n- 1 cycle/minute = 1/60 Hz = (1/60) × 10^6 μHz ≈ 16,667 μHz\n- So multiply by 1e6/60, not 1e6\n\nAlso **line 346**: `target_period_min = 60.0 / (target_freq_muhz * 1e-6)` \n- This computes: 60 / (1010e"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:26:30.898977+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:26:32.462790+00:00"}}

id: 1177
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1177, "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "data": {"id": "df4f90a3-ddd4-4118-9d9c-5e8867405716", "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "kind": "text", "position": 1173, "revision": 1177, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"text": "Good, I've read both sub-agent scripts. Now I can see the FFT unit error clearly:\n\n**Line 147**: `fft_freqs = np.fft.rfftfreq(n, d=dt)` where `dt` is in **minutes** → frequencies are in cycles/minute\n**Line 161**: `top_freqs_muhz = top_freqs_hz * 1e6` — treats cycles/minute as Hz and multiplies by 1e6\n\nThe correct conversion from cycles/minute to μHz:\n- 1 cycle/minute = 1/60 Hz = (1/60) × 10^6 μHz ≈ 16,667 μHz\n- So multiply by 1e6/60, not 1e6\n\nAlso **line 346**: `target_period_min = 60.0 / (target_freq_muhz * 1e-6)` \n- This computes: 60 / (1010e-6) = 59,406 minutes — wrong\n- Correct: period in seconds = 1/(freq_in_Hz) = 1/(1010e-6"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:26:30.898977+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:26:32.977876+00:00"}}

id: 1178
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1178, "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "data": {"id": "df4f90a3-ddd4-4118-9d9c-5e8867405716", "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "kind": "text", "position": 1173, "revision": 1178, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"text": "Good, I've read both sub-agent scripts. Now I can see the FFT unit error clearly:\n\n**Line 147**: `fft_freqs = np.fft.rfftfreq(n, d=dt)` where `dt` is in **minutes** → frequencies are in cycles/minute\n**Line 161**: `top_freqs_muhz = top_freqs_hz * 1e6` — treats cycles/minute as Hz and multiplies by 1e6\n\nThe correct conversion from cycles/minute to μHz:\n- 1 cycle/minute = 1/60 Hz = (1/60) × 10^6 μHz ≈ 16,667 μHz\n- So multiply by 1e6/60, not 1e6\n\nAlso **line 346**: `target_period_min = 60.0 / (target_freq_muhz * 1e-6)` \n- This computes: 60 / (1010e-6) = 59,406 minutes — wrong\n- Correct: period in seconds = 1/(freq_in_Hz) = 1/(1010e-6) = 990 s = 16.5 min\n\nLet me now write a corrected FFT analysis script and run it:\n\n"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:26:30.898977+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:26:33.497424+00:00"}}

