muHz) = [4374.3, 2291.3, 4790.9, 6457.3, 624.9], Nyquist=8227.8\n  Mean top peak across models: 4374.3 muHz\n\npass_11:\n  Model A: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [456.6, 684.9, 228.3, 913.2, 1826.5], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model B: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [4794.5, 6392.7, 2739.7, 5022.8, 7077.6], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model C: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [4794.5, 1598.2, 1826.5, 6392.7, 4566.2], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Mean top peak across models: 3348.6 muHz\n\npass_12:\n  Model A: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [625.0, 416.7, 1041.7, 833.3, 208.3], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model B: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [5000.0, 3125.0, 7916.7, 7500.0, 7291.7], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model C: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [5000.0, 3125.0, 625.0, 7916.7, 7500.0], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Mean top peak across models: 3541.7 muHz\n\npass_13:\n  Model A: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [273.2, 546.4, 819.7, 1366.1, 1092.9], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model B: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [6284.2, 5191.3, 7377.0, 7650.3, 6557.4], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model C: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [1092.9, 1366.1, 819.7, 6284.2, 5191.3], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Mean top peak across models: 2550.1 muHz\n\npass_14:\n  Model A: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [416.7, 833.3, 625.0, 1041.7, 1666.7], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model B: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [4791.7, 5000.0, 4583.3, 6666.7, 7708.3], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model C: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [1666.7, 1458.3, 2083.3, 1875.0, 4791.7], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Mean top peak across models: 2291.7 muHz\n\npass_15:\n  Model A: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [416.5, 624.8, 6039.7, 833.1, 1457.9], Nyquist=8122.4\n  Model B: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [6039.7, 8122.4, 3332.3, 7289.3, 4581.8], Nyquist=8122.4\n  Model C: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [6039.7, 8122.4, 3332.3, 7289.3, 4581.8], Nyquist=8122.4\n  Mean top peak across models: 4165.3 muHz\n\npass_16:\n  Model A: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [625.0, 1041.7, 5833.3, 416.7, 1666.7], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model B: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [7083.3, 5833.3, 3958.3, 7708.3, 5416.7], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model C: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [1666.7, 7083.3, 1041.7, 5833.3, 3958.3], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Mean top peak across models: 3125.0 muHz\n\npass_17:\n  Model A: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [625.0, 833.3, 416.7, 208.3, 1041.7], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model B: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [5208.3, 7916.7, 5416.7, 7083.3, 5000.0], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model C: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [833.3, 625.0, 5208.3, 7916.7, 5416.7], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Mean top peak across models: 2222.2 muHz\n\npass_18:\n  Model A: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [624.7, 832.9, 1041.2, 1249.4, 1457.6], Nyquist=8016.9\n  Model B: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [4581.1, 4372.8, 7288.1, 5622.2, 3748.2], Nyquist=8016.9\n  Model C: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [1665.8, 1457.6, 1249.4, 4581.1, 4372.8], Nyquist=8016.9\n  Mean top peak across models: 2290.5 muHz\n\npass_19:\n  Model A: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [456.3, 228.1, 3193.8, 2281.3, 912.5], Nyquist=7870.4\n  Model B: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [3193.8, 2281.3, 4334.4, 3421.9, 6843.8], Nyquist=7870.4\n  Model C: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [3193.8, 2281.3, 1368.8, 4334.4, 3421.9], Nyquist=7870.4\n  Mean top peak across models: 2281.3 muHz\n\npass_20:\n  Model A: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [625.0, 416.7, 833.3, 1041.7, 1250.0], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model B: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [6458.3, 3541.7, 7916.7, 4791.7, 2708.3], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model C: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [1458.3, 1666.7, 6458.3, 1250.0, 1041.7], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Mean top peak across models: 2847.2 muHz\n\npass_21:\n  Model A: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [416.7, 625.0, 1250.0, 1875.0, 208.3], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model B: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [6041.7, 3541.7, 8125.0, 2708.3, 2500.0], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model C: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [1250.0, 1875.0, 6041.7, 1458.3, 3541.7], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Mean top peak across models: 2569.4 muHz\n\npass_22:\n  Model A: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [416.7, 833.3, 1458.3, 625.0, 2291.7], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model B: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [2291.7, 1875.0, 2500.0, 7291.7, 2083.3], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Model C: top-5 freqs (muHz) = [1458.3, 833.3, 2291.7, 1666.7, 1041.7], Nyquist=8333.3\n  Mean top peak across models: 1388.9 muHz\n\nCross-pass consistency:\n  Total passes: 22\n  Has consistent signal (>half passes): True\n  Top 10 frequencies across all passes:\n    620 muHz: 23 appearances\n    830 muHz: 19 appearances\n    1040 muHz: 17 appearances\n    420 muHz: 14 appearances\n    1670 muHz: 11 appearances\n    1250 muHz: 10 appearances\n    1460 muHz: 10 appearances\n    4580 muHz: 9 appearances\n    4790 muHz: 9 appearances\n    2080 muHz: 8 appearances\n\n============================================================\n2. CANDIDATE SPECTRUM CONSISTENCY (CORRECTED)\n============================================================\n\nRank-1 parameters: {'candidate_rank': 1, 'max_velocity_cm_s': 30.0, 'min_velocity_cm_s': 0.05, 'peak_frequency_microhz': 1010.0, 'frequency_width_microhz': 275.0, 'delta_information_criterion': 0.0}\nRank-1 in spectrum comparison: False\nTarget frequency: 1010.0 muHz = 0.00101 Hz\nTarget period: 990.1 seconds = 16.5 minutes\nPasses that can resolve target freq: 22/22\nPasses with target freq within window: 22/22\n  pass_01: span=79.0 min, nyquist=8333.3 muHz, can_resolve=True, in_window=True\n  pass_02: span=79.0 min, nyquist=7489.5 muHz, can_resolve=True, in_window=True\n  pass_22: span=79.0 min, nyquist=8333.3 muHz, can_resolve=True, in_window=True\n\nSaved corrected FFT results to [workspace]\nSaved corrected consistency results to [workspace]\n\n============================================================\nFINAL SUMMARY\n============================================================\nNumber of passes analyzed: 22\nConsistent FFT peak found: True\n  Common signal at 620 muHz (23 passes)\n  Common signal at 830 muHz (19 passes)\n  Common signal at 1040 muHz (17 passes)\n  Common signal at 420 muHz (14 passes)\nTarget period for 1010 muHz: 16.5 minutes\nPasses with target freq resolvable: 22/22\nPasses with target freq within analysis window: 22/22", "status": "completed", "is_async": false, "tool_use_id": "call_14315932696b4ee6b076b1df"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:27:06.610495+00:00