id: 1278
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1278, "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "data": {"id": "8f3a7803-c568-47cd-89ee-06cdedd05901", "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "kind": "text", "position": 1278, "revision": 1278, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"text": "**Validation passes: `passed: true`, 0 errors, 0 warnings.** All 5 findings have resolvable analysis sources and result evidence.\n\n## Round 003 Corrections Summary\n\n### Sub-Agent Scripts Read\n- `working/subagent_fft_loo/fft_loo_analysis.py` — read (identified unit conversion error at lines 147, 161, 346)\n- `working/subagent_verification/independent_verification.py` —"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:28:41.508932+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:28:41.508939+00:00"}}

id: 1279
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1279, "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "data": {"id": "8f3a7803-c568-47cd-89ee-06cdedd05901", "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "kind": "text", "position": 1278, "revision": 1279, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"text": "**Validation passes: `passed: true`, 0 errors, 0 warnings.** All 5 findings have resolvable analysis sources and result evidence.\n\n## Round 003 Corrections Summary\n\n### Sub-Agent Scripts Read\n- `working/subagent_fft_loo/fft_loo_analysis.py` — read (identified unit conversion error at lines 147, 161, 346)\n- `working/subagent_verification/independent_verification.py` — read (verified correctness)\n\n### FFT Unit Correction Applied\n| Error | Original | Corrected |\n|-------|----------|-----------|\n| Frequency conversion | `cycles/minute * 1e6` (factor of 60 too high) | `dt in seconds → rfftfreq → Hz * 1e6 = μHz` |\n| Nyquist frequency | Claimed up to 487,500 μHz (impossible) | **8,333 μHz** (correct for 1-min sampling) |\n| Target period | 59,400 minutes (wrong formula) | **16.5 minutes** (1/0.00101 Hz / 60) |\n|"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:28:41.508932+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:28:42.030968+00:00"}}

id: 1280
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1280, "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "data": {"id": "8f3a7803-c568-47cd-89ee-06cdedd05901", "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "kind": "text", "position": 1278, "revision": 1280, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"text": "**Validation passes: `passed: true`, 0 errors, 0 warnings.** All 5 findings have resolvable analysis sources and result evidence.\n\n## Round 003 Corrections Summary\n\n### Sub-Agent Scripts Read\n- `working/subagent_fft_loo/fft_loo_analysis.py` — read (identified unit conversion error at lines 147, 161, 346)\n- `working/subagent_verification/independent_verification.py` — read (verified correctness)\n\n### FFT Unit Correction Applied\n| Error | Original | Corrected |\n|-------|----------|-----------|\n| Frequency conversion | `cycles/minute * 1e6` (factor of 60 too high) | `dt in seconds → rfftfreq → Hz * 1e6 = μHz` |\n| Nyquist frequency | Claimed up to 487,500 μHz (impossible) | **8,333 μHz** (correct for 1-min sampling) |\n| Target period | 59,400 minutes (wrong formula) | **16.5 minutes** (1/0.00101 Hz / 60) |\n| Resolution claim | \"no pass can resolve 1010 μHz\" | **All 22 passes can resolve it** (Nyquist >> 1010, window >> 16.5 min) |\n| Peak detection | \"no consistent signal near 1010 μHz\" | **1040 μHz appears as top-5 peak in 17/22 passes** |\n\n### Scientific Impact\nFinding 1 headline changed from \"**Not Confirmed by Temporal Periodicity"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:28:41.508932+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:28:42.552419+00:00"}}

id: 1282
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1282, "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "data": {"id": "8f3a7803-c568-47cd-89ee-06cdedd05901", "run_id": "run_019c2e0ca17d4274", "kind": "text", "position": 1278, "revision": 1282, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"text": "**Validation passes: `passed: true`, 0 errors, 0 warnings.** All 5 findings have resolvable analysis sources and result evidence.\n\n## Round 003 Corrections Summary\n\n### Sub-Agent Scripts Read\n- `working/subagent_fft_loo/fft_loo_analysis.py` — read (identified unit conversion error at lines 147, 161, 346)\n- `working/subagent_verification/independent_verification.py` — read (verified correctness)\n\n### FFT Unit Correction Applied\n| Error | Original | Corrected |\n|-------|----------|-----------|\n| Frequency conversion | `cycles/minute * 1e6` (factor of 60 too high) | `dt in seconds → rfftfreq → Hz * 1e6 = μHz` |\n| Nyquist frequency | Claimed up to 487,500 μHz (impossible) | **8,333 μHz** (correct for 1-min sampling) |\n| Target period | 59,400 minutes (wrong formula) | **16.5 minutes** (1/0.00101 Hz / 60) |\n| Resolution claim | \"no pass can resolve 1010 μHz\" | **All 22 passes can resolve it** (Nyquist >> 1010, window >> 16.5 min) |\n| Peak detection | \"no consistent signal near 1010 μHz\" | **1040 μHz appears as top-5 peak in 17/22 passes** |\n\n### Scientific Impact\nFinding 1 headline changed from \"**Not Confirmed by Temporal Periodicity Analysis**\" to \"**Supported by Both IC Ranking and Independent FFT Periodicity Analysis**\". The corrected FFT confirms that the data have sufficient temporal resolution to detect the preferred frequency, and 1040 μHz is a consistently prominent peak across most passes.\n\n### Artifacts Updated\n- `output/result_artifacts.json` — replaced mislabeled FFT with corrected version\n- `working/analysis-state.md` — updated to r4 with all corrections logged\n- `working/subagent_fft_loo_corrected/` — contains corrected FFT script and results"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:28:41.508932+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:28:43.030445+00:00"}}

